invariant: INV-50
file: sha512.c
catches: hash_runtime_test
reason: sha512.c picks its first arm on a macro no build defines, so a host
  object compiles the second arm, a device object's, and every SHA-384
  call that no kernel takes compresses on sha512_compress.c's function.
  Every digest is right, because that function is the reference, so no
  vector, no equivalence case and no proof sees it; only the time is
  wrong, by the factor docs/decisions.md 127 measures, and the stack
  below each call is no longer wiped. The design refuses a silent fall
  back: a host object is a statement about what the object contains.
  bin/hash_runtime_test counts the calls into each compression function
  and requires that the reference took none.

--- old
#ifdef CH_CPU_RUNTIME

#include <string.h>

#include "ct.h"
--- new
#ifdef CH_SHA512_COMPRESS_BLOCKS

#include <string.h>

#include "ct.h"
